From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:18:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: meson: odroid-go-ultra: add red charging LED

The red LED on the back of the ODROID-GO Ultra (left of the power LED)
is driven by GPIOAO_6, active high, but it is not described in the
mainline device tree, so it never lights under Linux.

Add it to the gpio-leds node with the battery power supply's
charging-blink-full-solid trigger: it blinks while charging and stays
on when the battery is full.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts
index cebedab..7554cf3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts
@@ -220,6 +220,13 @@
 	leds {
 		compatible = "gpio-leds";
 
+		led-red {
+			color = <LED_COLOR_ID_RED>;
+			function = LED_FUNCTION_CHARGING;
+			gpios = <&gpio_ao GPIOAO_6 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			linux,default-trigger = "battery-charging-blink-full-solid";
+		};
+
 		led-blue {
 			color = <LED_COLOR_ID_BLUE>;
 			gpios = <&gpio_ao GPIOAO_11 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
-- 
